\0
Several years after the Freedom Guard destroyed the Dessicator weapon on Corlbad, Imperium scientists were able to duplicate the weapon. In order to avoid losing the weapon again, the Dessicator was developed as a series of components on a number of worlds. All aspects of the research were duplicated, and only General Trilkin was aware of the sites of all phases of development.  When all was ready, Imperium fleets brought the separate components to Monat for final implementation. 
\1
The Imperium has produced another Dessicator on Monat. If they can bring the weapon's force to bear, we cannot withstand them. We don't know where the weapon is housed, so you will have to destroy everything until you find it. Leave nothing standing.
\n\n
\cOBJECTIVES\n
\n
--> Destroy all Imperium structures
\2
The final conflict is at hand. The strength of your will is obvious. It will serve you well.\n
\n
\cHISTORICAL OUTCOME:\n
A desperate Freedom Guard ground assault failed to take the heavily fortified Imperium position. The invading force was devastated, and the Dessicator remained intact. Imperium General Trilkin's command fleet took the Dessicator and moved towards Strata, the Freedom Guard's largest remaining stronghold, where they would use the devastating weapon.
\3
Many lives depend on you. You are too close to fail now.


